    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d631">

                <pb facs="0854" n="842" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg842"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856E.00/8–3046: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Batavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Foote</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Batavia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-30T16:00:00+07:30">August 30, 1946—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 30—3:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>350. Mytel 348, August 27.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d631-f1"/> After Killearn
                    received invitation from Sjahrir through Hadji Agoes Salim<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d631-f2"/> to visit Djocjakarta he changed plans and went Djocja
                    early yesterday morning by RAF plane to stay
                    only 2 hours but he talked with Sjahrir about 5 hours, returned <pb facs="0855"
                        n="843" xml:id="pg843"/> Batavia same day and returned Singapore by air this
                    morning. Before taking off, he sent for me and gave following re Djocja
                    trip:</p>
                <p>He impressed on Indonesians need for immediate truce, is hopeful that it will be
                    arranged and asked General Mansergh to send plane for Indonesian officers to
                    negotiate it; he told Indonesians British troops will leave NEI by end of
                    November and impressed on them necessity for resumption of negotiations. He then
                    told me he will return Batavia after arrival Schermerhorn so that negotiations
                    may be hastened as much as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foote</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d631-f1" n="9" xml:id="d631-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported the arrival from Singapore of Lord Killearn, British
                    Special Commissioner in Southeast Asia (856E.00/8–2746).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d631-f2" n="10" xml:id="d631-f2-content">
                <p>Vice Minister for Foreign Affairs in the new Cabinet headed by Soetan
                    Sjahrir.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
